etween stores — moving a plan from markdown\nto SQLite is a seed, and a seed is a command sequence the contract already has (and\n`seed::from_manifest` now accepts any `CommandService`).\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone outstanding.\n","owner":"store","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:planning-store-as-backend"},{"depends_on":"story:events-reach-the-store"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"open enumerates and folds what the store holds, installing stored identities; needs entity-runtime's store enumeration; the written-set refusal is deleted.","tags":["backend","store"],"title":"A populated database is read back on open, and the foreign-row refusal retires"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"},"owner":"store","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:planning-store-as-backend"},{"depends_on":"story:events-reach-the-store"}],"summary":"open enumerates and folds what the store holds, installing stored identities; needs entity-runtime's store enumeration; the written-set refusal is deleted.","tags":["backend","store"],"title":"A populated database is read back on open, and the foreign-row refusal retires"},"id":"ent-44d2630d193a6e5cea82d9676bbeb9c1","lifecycle_state":"implemented","revision":9,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["story","ent-44d2630d193a6e5cea82d9676bbeb9c1"]}]